  "turn": 1,
  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "**TX-0401 amount verified: EUR 240.00**\n\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Type:** Card payment, outgoing, status settled\n- **Account:** ACC-1005\n\nI see another charge from the same merchant for the same amount: **TX-0402, EUR 240.00 on 2026-07-14**, also settled. That may be relevant depending on what happened.\n\nThese are the dispute reason codes that could apply to a card payment like this:\n\n1. **duplicate_charge**: You were charged more than once for the same purchase. TX-0402 matches TX-0401 in merchant and amount, so this code may fit if both charges were for one order.\n2. **fraud_card_not_present**: You did not authorise an online card payment and did not make it yourself.\n3. **unauthorized_debit**: The debit was taken from your account without your authorisation.\n4. **goods_not_received**: You paid for something that was never delivered.\n5. **service_not_rendered**: You paid for a service that was never provided.\n\nI have not opened a dispute. Before filing, I need you to tell me what happened so I can identify the right code. I will then run an eligibility check first, and I will only open the dispute if that check passes.",
